WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.525
In impromptu speaking, the hardest part is often choosing.

00:00:03.525 --> 00:00:08.084
Read the prompt, decide what it suggests, and write a one sentence message.

00:00:08.084 --> 00:00:11.002
You do not need the most unusual interpretation.

00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:15.135
You need an interpretation you can explain with clarity and purpose.

00:00:16.335 --> 00:00:18.497
Use a structure you can remember.

00:00:18.497 --> 00:00:24.068
Open with your central idea, develop two examples, and return to the idea at the end.

00:00:24.068 --> 00:00:27.082
Explain how each example supports the message.

00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:31.800
An anecdote without analysis is a story, but not yet a persuasive point.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.920
Impromptu rules vary across leagues and tournaments.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.346
Check the preparation and speaking limits before you compete.

00:00:39.346 --> 00:00:42.940
In practice, use one minute to prepare and two minutes to speak.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:49.005
Afterwards, ask whether a listener could summarize your message and describe how your
examples supported it.
